070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399461 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,-4,2⟩$, $c=⟨3,-10,2⟩$, and  $u=⟨-2,5,0⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399461 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "da64bb93-914e-5229-bb6d-b7d97e6fa1bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399461 #edb/ref 1074 "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}s+3t=-2 \\\\ -4s-10t=5 \\\\ 2s+2t=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -10 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-2,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399462 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399462 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399462 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399462 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 175921